.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KUBE-NETWORK 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kube-network
.Nd make this machine a node of the kldload WireGuard mesh, on its management and Kubernetes planes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm init
.Ar node-id
.Op Fl -force
.Nm
.Cm add-peer
.Ar endpoint pubkey peer-id
.Nm
.Cm remove-peer
.Ar peer-id
.Nm
.Cm show-keys | status | pin-kubelet | nft
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The kldload mesh has two WireGuard planes:
.Ql wg-mgmt ,
.Ql 10.250.0. Ns Ar id ,
port 51820, for ssh, management and monitoring; and
.Ql wg-k8s ,
.Ql 10.251.0. Ns Ar id ,
port 51821, for the kubelet, the API server and pod traffic.
Every node has one id, 1 to 254, and the same address on both planes.
.Xr kube-cluster 8
gives the control plane 1 and workers 2 up, the hypervisor is 100, and
.Xr kldload-enroll 8
gives other machines 150 up.
.Pp
.Nm
is the node's half: it makes the keys and configurations, adds and
removes peers, and brings the interfaces up under
.Ql wg-quick@ ,
checking afterwards that they are.
It runs itself under
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm init Ar node-id Op Fl -force
Make the keys and both configurations and bring them up.
A node that already has a configuration is left alone \(em a second
.Cm init
would drop every peer it has \(em unless
.Fl -force
is given to re-key it or move it to another id.
.It Cm add-peer Ar endpoint pubkey peer-id
Add a peer to both planes, at
.Ar endpoint
on each plane's port, and reload them.
.Ar endpoint
must be an address or host name,
.Ar pubkey
a WireGuard public key, and
.Ar peer-id
1 to 254.
.It Cm remove-peer Ar peer-id
Remove it from both planes; a peer that is not there is not an error.
.It Cm show-keys
This node's id and public keys.
.It Cm status
.Ql wg show
for both planes.
.It Cm pin-kubelet
Make the kubelet use this node's
.Ql wg-k8s
address, and restart it if a cluster is running.
.It Cm nft
Replace the whole
.Xr nft 8
ruleset with one for a Kubernetes node: established traffic, ssh, the
WireGuard ports, everything on the two planes, the node's own subnet and
the pod network, the API server and the NodePort range; everything else
dropped.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev K8S_POD_CIDR
The pod network
.Cm nft
trusts; default
.Ql 10.244.0.0/16 .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/wireguard/wg-mgmt.conf , Pa /etc/wireguard/wg-k8s.conf
The planes, mode 0600; they hold the private key.
.It Pa /etc/wireguard/wg-mgmt.key , Pa .pub , Pa wg-k8s.key , Pa .pub
The keys.
.It Pa /etc/wireguard/.node-id
This node's id.
.It Pa /etc/default/kubelet
Written by
.Cm pin-kubelet .
.It Pa /etc/nftables.conf
Written by
.Cm nft .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when done; 1 when a step failed or a value was refused, named; 2 on a
usage error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
