.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-enroll 8 ,
.Xr kube-cluster 8 ,
.Xr wg 8 ,
.Xr wg-quick 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-08-16 a control plane carried 17 peers where 8 were right: there
was no way to remove one.
On 2026-08-24 an enrolment sweep ran
.Cm init
on every node every ten minutes and flattened a six-node mesh to one
peer each, while every node stayed Ready.
On 2026-08-31 a node whose configurations had been deleted kept its id
file, and
.Cm init
did nothing and succeeded.
On 2026-09-27 a peer added to an interface deleted by hand reported
success with no interface.
.Pp
On 2026-09-30, writing this page, in a container:
.Cm add-peer
wrote its arguments into the configurations unchecked, so a newline in
one, or a peer id of
.Ql 08 ,
left configurations that would not load and both planes down;
.Cm remove-peer
copied the configuration, private key included, through
.Pa /tmp .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
One key serves both planes: the two public keys are the same, and
.Cm add-peer
takes one.
.Pp
.Cm nft
flushes every rule on the machine, the hypervisor's and container
runtime's among them; it is for a Kubernetes node, not the host its
virtual machines run on.
